Angular multi entry points library - referencing scss file from other entry point

I have created an Angular (v22) library with 2 entry points, and need to use a shared scss in both entry points.

The library is build with ng-packagr

The file structure looks like this (simplified):

Workspace folder
{
  angular.json
  tsconfig.json
  package.json
  projects
  {
    core
    {
      index.ts
      ng-package.json
      package.json
      tsconfig.core.json
      logo-spinner
      {
        index.ts
        ng-package.json
        src
        {
          public-api.ts
          lib
          {
            logo-spinner.component.ts
            logo-spinner.component.scss
          }
        }
      }
      accept-dialog
      {
        index.ts
        ng-package.json
        src
        {
          public-api.ts
          lib
          {
            accept-dialog.component.ts
            accept-dialog.component.scss
          }
        }
      }
      assets
      {
        styles
        {
          main.scss
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

My problem is how to access the 'library global' main.scss from the stylesheets in the libraries entry point's style files.

I have tried to add variations of @use in logo-spinner.component.scss as follows:

@use "assets/styles/main";

@use "main";

@use "@core/main";

but nothing works.

The ts files are linked by the public-api.ts and index.ts files, but it seems, I am missing something similar for the style mappings.

None of all the webpages I have read, deal with this, so if you know, then please enlighten me.

Michael

